/Title (The National Service Scheme \(NSS\), Youth Red Cross \(YRC\), and Red Ribbon Club \(RRC\) organized a Blood Donation Camp on 31 July 2026 in collaboration with Meenakshi Mission Hospital, Madurai. More than 50 students and staff members voluntarily registered for the camp, and 40 units of blood were collected. Doctors, nurses, and medical technicians guided the participants throughout the donation process and created awareness about the importance and safety of blood donation. Certificates were distributed to the donors as a token of appreciation, and the programme promoted social responsibility and a spirit of service among the student community. The programme was coordinated by Mr. C. Balaguru, AP/Mech, RRC Coordinator & Mr. R. Rajendran, AP/Civil, YRC Coordinator.)
